---
description: Rust coding standards (ALFDF MVP0 spec + workspace lints)
globs: crates/**/*.rs
alwaysApply: false
---

- Rust 2024; workspace `[workspace.lints]` / crate-root `#![warn(...)]` per pinned stack ([05-tech-stack.mdc](05-tech-stack.mdc)).
- Function ≤ 100 LOC; module ≤ 500 LOC. Split before exceeding.
- No unwrap/expect outside tests or `# Panics`-documented items.
- No unsafe without `// SAFETY:`.
- Public items: rustdoc with what/why + ≥1 example.
- Module header `//!` answers "This module is responsible for …" in ≤12 words
  and cites the `.DOCS/ALFDF-MVP0-Project-Spec-v0.1.md` section it implements (e.g. §3 ABAL, §8 storage).
- thiserror for libs; anyhow only in future MVP1 `alfdf` CLI (§17 — not in MVP0 library crates).
- Trait method count ≤ 5 (SOLID-I).
- rustfmt: max_width=100, group_imports=StdExternalCrate.
